        "summary":  "The article introduces the Agent Evaluation Metric (AEM), a framework for evaluating AI agent quality in multi-turn conversations by decomposing performance into named sub-metrics measured turn-by-turn. AEM addresses the problem where early errors cascade through subsequent turns, obscuring root causes — instead of a single task-level score, it provides truthfulness and completeness measurements that identify precisely which turn and dimension caused failures. The methodology includes error attribution to separate root causes from downstream effects and integrates with existing evaluation pipelines like Strands Agents.",
        "execSummary":  "AWS has published a structured evaluation methodology — the Agent Evaluation Metric — that breaks down AI agent quality in multi-turn conversations to the turn and dimension level, rather than relying on a single pass/fail task score. This is directly decision-relevant for any enterprise deploying AI agents in customer-service or support contexts, where a single misunderstanding early in a conversation can compound into a failed resolution. The framework\u0027s ability to isolate root causes (e.g., a retrieval failure vs. a reasoning failure) gives operations and quality teams an actionable diagnostic tool, not just a scorecard. Teams building or evaluating agent deployments should adopt a similar decomposed evaluation approach before scaling, as aggregate scores routinely mask the failure modes that matter most to customers.",
