        "source":  "InfoWorld",
        "url":  "https://www.infoworld.com/article/4220288/why-enterprises-should-start-with-on-site-ai-agents.html",
        "date":  "2026-09-10",
        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "The article argues that enterprises should prioritize building AI agents that operate on their own websites rather than deploying browser extensions or cloud-based agents. On-site agents provide full governance, accountability, and brand control, while external agents create compliance and security risks despite offering greater reach. Regulated industries in particular are advised to establish internal governance foundations before expanding agent capabilities outward.",
        "execSummary":  "Enterprise leaders should build AI agents on their own digital properties first, prioritizing governance and accountability over reach and scale. Off-site and in-browser agents, while promising discovery and scale, operate outside business control — creating regulatory exposure when they misquote prices, misstate policies, or initiate unauthorized transactions. On-site agents provide auditable interactions with explicit tool contracts, enabling regulated industries to maintain brand integrity and compliance while building operational competence with agent systems. This foundation allows responsible outward expansion only after internal governance is proven and measurable.",
